How would you debug a pod stuck in “ContainerCreating” during deployment? What are your next 3 CLI commands? 
 
A pod stuck in ContainerCreating usually means Kubernetes is struggling to provision storage, pull the container image, or configure the network. 

1. we need to Inspect the Pod Lifecycle Events 

kubectl describe pod <pod-name> -n <namespace> 

2. we need to check Cluster-Wide Resource Constraints  

kubectl get nodes 

3. we need to check Infrastructure and Storage Status

kubectl get pvc,pv -n <namespace>
  
